 "population": "exposed_development_only",
 "notes": "Exploratory development-only population for measuring whether the primary endpoint L (terminal loss of a protected goal) is ever non-degenerate under the outcome-blind public trigger v3. These 32 tasks are the complete subset of the 2285 pinned telecom tasks that (a) carry a user-side coupled mobile-data goal (assert_mobile_data_status / assert_internet_speed), (b) are abroad with carrier roaming pre-enabled at initialization (assistant enable_roaming in initialization_actions) and device roaming turned off, and (c) have NO assistant WRITE in their reference solution (purely user-fixable via device toggles). This is the only task structure in the domain where a coupled goal can be FALSE initially yet TRUE at root capture via user-only prefix actions (hence protectable), so that a reviewer-selected disable_roaming could regress it via environment.py roaming_allowed coupling. Selection used task metadata only (env_assertion func_name/env_type, initialization_actions, reference-solution requestor/name); no model calls and no outcome labels.",
 "selection_rule": "exhaustive scan of pinned tasks.json; include iff user-side coupled mobile-data assertion present AND set_user_location(abroad=true) AND assistant enable_roaming in initialization_actions AND turn_roaming_off in initialization_actions AND zero assistant WRITE actions in evaluation_criteria.actions",
